// Two `when` clauses on one rule.
//
// New idea: a rule may carry multiple Cedar `when` clauses.
// They are AND-ed together — the rule fires only if every
// `when` body evaluates to true.

permit(
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"SellShares",
    resource
)
when { context.input.shares < 100 }
when { context.input.stock == "AMZN" };
